00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:33.830
<b>Alps no Shoujo Heidi</b>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
<u>Why do I hear</u>

00:00:33.900 --> 00:00:36.090
Kuchibue ha naze

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
<u>the whistling from far away?</u>

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.250
Tooku made kikoeru no

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
<u>Why is that cloud</u>

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.460
Ano kumo ha naze

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
<u>waiting for me?</u>

00:00:40.470 --> 00:00:42.600
Watashi wo matteru no

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:42.840 --> 00:00:46.800
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
<u>Tell me, Grandfather.</u>

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:50.690
Oshiete ojiisan

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
<u>Oh tell me, the fir trees of the Alm.</u>

00:00:50.860 --> 00:00:59.380
Oshiete arumu no momi no ki yo

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:26.630
Where is Pichi?

00:01:29.900 --> 00:01:32.960
Heidi has stopped going to the mountain pastures.

00:01:33.110 --> 00:01:35.990
A short fall has come to the Alm Mountain.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:40.330
The newly fallen snow
makes the mountain peaks sparkle.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.920
Good morning!
Where is Heidi?

00:01:54.930 --> 00:01:56.340
She is still sleeping.

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:04.490
Pichi!
Why didn't he wake me up?

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:12.940
Grandfather, good morning!

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:16.610
Good morning.
You woke up late today.

00:02:16.770 --> 00:02:19.970
Because Pichi didn't wake me up.

00:02:19.970 --> 00:02:23.160
Now that you mention it,
I haven't seen him yet today.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.220
Good morning, Peter!
Did you see Pichi?

00:02:27.230 --> 00:02:28.000
No.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:28.920
I see.

00:02:29.120 --> 00:02:31.160
Did something happen to him?

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:34.070
He didn't wake me up this morning.

00:02:34.970 --> 00:02:38.740
Maybe he got fed up because
you didn't wake up, and left.

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:43.010
Well, I see you later!

00:02:56.600 --> 00:02:57.980
Pichi!

00:02:58.300 --> 00:03:00.010
Pichi!

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.970
Pichi!

00:03:14.640 --> 00:03:16.220
How did it go?

00:03:16.810 --> 00:03:18.440
I can't find him anywhere.

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:20.200
Really?

00:03:28.850 --> 00:03:32.450
Grandfather, why hasn't Pichi come?

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:35.430
Well, I don't know.

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:42.350
Here!

00:03:44.670 --> 00:03:47.380
Here. Let's see if you can
make something with these.

00:03:54.320 --> 00:03:55.190
What is it?

00:03:58.210 --> 00:03:59.210
It's Pichi!

00:04:06.690 --> 00:04:08.300
It's not Pichi.

00:04:15.430 --> 00:04:16.390
Pichi!

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:22.800
Pichi, why didn't you wake me up this morning?

00:04:23.150 --> 00:04:24.700
I was worried about you!

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:28.210
What's wrong?
Pichi, come back!

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:32.040
Pichi!

00:04:32.440 --> 00:04:33.920
Pichi!

00:04:34.710 --> 00:04:36.280
Pichi!

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.500
Pichi!

00:04:48.860 --> 00:04:51.040
Wait, Pichi!

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:52.300
Heidi!

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:00.560
Joseph.

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:10.410
Pichi!

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.790
Where are you going, Pichi?
Wait for me!

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:30.030
Pichi! Pichi!

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:33.680
Pichi!

00:05:41.600 --> 00:05:42.780
Pichi!

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:46.670
Pichi!

00:06:39.160 --> 00:06:41.490
I'd better send Joseph after her.

00:06:43.060 --> 00:06:44.250
Joseph!

00:07:57.500 --> 00:07:58.950
Joseph!

00:08:12.120 --> 00:08:13.590
Joseph...

00:08:13.860 --> 00:08:16.720
Why did Pichi go away?

00:08:18.690 --> 00:08:21.790
Is it because I slept too much?

00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.520
I don't think it was because of that.

00:08:26.560 --> 00:08:28.800
I'm sure there must be another reason.

00:08:39.520 --> 00:08:41.220
Joseph, let's go home.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:56.110
Snowflake!

00:08:56.700 --> 00:08:58.000
Did you come alone again?

00:08:58.080 --> 00:08:59.580
You can't do that!

00:08:58.730 --> 00:09:00.150
Snowflake!

00:09:00.920 --> 00:09:01.920
Snowflake.

00:09:02.150 --> 00:09:03.400
Peter!

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:05.540
Don't run away.

00:09:05.630 --> 00:09:07.560
Why are you already here?

00:09:08.140 --> 00:09:10.760
The weather is getting worse.
That's why I've come back.

00:09:10.850 --> 00:09:11.760
Really?

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:16.790
Heidi! Can you tell me
what are you doing here?

00:09:16.880 --> 00:09:18.730
I came looking for Pichi.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:21.410
And did you find him?

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:28.240
Why do you think Pichi decided to leave?

00:09:28.670 --> 00:09:32.290
Like I said, he was tired of
waiting for you to wake up.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:36.200
That's not true! He came
every day until yesterday!

00:09:36.600 --> 00:09:39.150
Then maybe he doesn't like you anymore.

00:09:39.590 --> 00:09:42.720
That's a lie!
Because I'm his best friend!

00:09:42.840 --> 00:09:44.640
Then why did he went away?

00:09:44.640 --> 00:09:46.440
I told you I don't know!

00:09:46.930 --> 00:09:48.330
It's because he doesn't like you.

00:09:48.330 --> 00:09:49.340
You're wrong!

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:54.660
It's all right, isn't it?
Why he went away doesn't matter.

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.190
It matters!

00:09:57.950 --> 00:10:01.020
Heck! Birds have wings, you know!
It's obvious he flew away!

00:10:02.790 --> 00:10:04.910
Peter, that's mean.

00:10:04.910 --> 00:10:06.010
I hate you!

00:10:10.110 --> 00:10:12.340
Why is she so angry?

00:10:19.630 --> 00:10:22.550
Welcome back.
How did it go?

00:10:40.640 --> 00:10:44.230
I see. You brought him up
with such special care.

00:10:54.100 --> 00:10:56.890
Come on, Heidi. Don't cry anymore.

00:11:01.090 --> 00:11:03.730
Why did Pichi leave?

00:11:03.970 --> 00:11:05.970
Is it because he hates me?

00:11:06.660 --> 00:11:09.110
No, no. It's not because of that.

00:11:09.260 --> 00:11:14.570
I'm sure it's because winter is coming,
and he went looking for a warmer place.

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:16.670
A warmer place?

00:11:17.640 --> 00:11:24.730
Pichi loves you, but birds can't live in
the mountains when it's cold.

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:35.800
It's much better for him to go look for a warmer
place with his friends, than staying here.

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:41.190
So Pichi has flown away
with the other birds?

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.330
So that's why, Pichi...

00:11:48.980 --> 00:11:50.080
But...

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:54.020
Then why don't you live with the other people?

00:11:55.790 --> 00:11:58.580
People are like birds, aren't they?

00:12:04.080 --> 00:12:10.710
There are many kinds of birds, Heidi.
The hawk lives alone, doesn't it?

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:13.390
Then you are like a hawk?

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:20.420
Grandfather is not alone.
I live together with you, Heidi.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:23.120
Joseph, too.

00:12:25.720 --> 00:12:30.860
Well, cheer up.
I'm sure Pichi will be back in spring.

00:12:30.860 --> 00:12:32.980
Really? He will return?

00:12:33.610 --> 00:12:35.770
Yes, with all his friends.

00:12:37.640 --> 00:12:39.820
I hope spring comes fast!

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:42.500
Don't you think, Grandfather?

00:12:43.170 --> 00:12:44.940
You're very impatient.

00:13:12.240 --> 00:13:14.140
What is it, Goat General?

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:15.860
Where is Heidi?

00:13:15.860 --> 00:13:17.440
She's inside.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:21.560
She's still angry?

00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:23.500
Who knows?

00:13:23.500 --> 00:13:26.430
She didn't come out, so she must be.

00:13:36.110 --> 00:13:38.900
Hey, General! What are you waiting for?

00:13:39.560 --> 00:13:42.740
Look, your soldiers are going ahead of you.

00:13:49.690 --> 00:13:50.870
Then, I'm going.

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:02.250
Why didn't you come out to see Peter?

00:14:03.630 --> 00:14:05.690
He cares about you.

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:07.780
Because that Peter...

00:14:08.800 --> 00:14:10.590
Understood, understood.

00:14:10.880 --> 00:14:12.460
By the way, Heidi.

00:14:12.460 --> 00:14:15.370
Today I will take you to a nice place.

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.540
To a nice place?

00:14:43.210 --> 00:14:44.360
I know.

00:14:50.240 --> 00:14:51.220
Take that.

00:14:59.730 --> 00:15:01.480
Wait!

00:15:01.480 --> 00:15:03.900
Wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:15:07.600 --> 00:15:09.350
I said, wait!

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:12.610
All right, take that!

00:15:23.890 --> 00:15:27.010
Of course there are none.
They've grown into young birds by now.

00:15:32.500 --> 00:15:33.650
Stop that!

00:15:56.120 --> 00:15:58.980
Grandfather, where are we going?
Where is the nice place?

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:00.600
What are we going to do there?

00:16:03.180 --> 00:16:04.740
We're going to pick Chestnuts.

00:16:05.980 --> 00:16:09.940
And that's not all.
We're also going to pick currants.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.100
Really?

00:16:11.800 --> 00:16:15.310
Grandfather has a secret
place that only he knows.

00:16:16.640 --> 00:16:19.220
A secret place?
Peter doesn't know about it?

00:16:19.410 --> 00:16:20.510
Of course not.

00:16:21.030 --> 00:16:25.120
If he knew about it,
he would eat everything.

00:16:36.550 --> 00:16:38.040
Like this.

00:17:26.550 --> 00:17:29.770
Come flying, come flying.
Hurry and come flying.

00:17:44.230 --> 00:17:46.570
Hey, Greenfinch!
Go away!

00:17:47.910 --> 00:17:49.170
If you go there...!

00:17:50.670 --> 00:17:53.290
Stop that! Go, go, go!
Curses!

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:55.670
Idiot!

00:17:57.210 --> 00:17:58.620
Snowflake, wait!

00:17:59.340 --> 00:18:00.090
Hey!

00:18:02.840 --> 00:18:03.460
Wait!

00:18:11.440 --> 00:18:12.800
You can't do that!

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:14.040
Come here!

00:18:20.490 --> 00:18:22.330
Next time I'll hit you!

00:18:30.730 --> 00:18:31.730
It escaped.

00:18:33.560 --> 00:18:35.430
Damn!

00:18:54.270 --> 00:18:55.980
There's so many!

00:18:56.570 --> 00:18:59.420
Peter will be so surprised when he sees this.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:03.430
But Peter can't know about this place.

00:19:03.530 --> 00:19:08.530
Of course. Why would I tell
such a silly boy about this place?

00:19:11.950 --> 00:19:13.660
What is that, grandfather?

00:19:14.910 --> 00:19:17.080
You'll understand if you go inside.

00:19:18.670 --> 00:19:20.080
{++++Behind that?}In there?

00:19:25.020 --> 00:19:26.370
Amazing!

00:19:30.560 --> 00:19:34.320
Peter will be so surprised when he sees this.

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:48.280
Grandfather, your beard!

00:19:49.400 --> 00:19:50.740
It's red.

00:19:52.700 --> 00:19:54.030
You, too, Heidi.

00:20:09.500 --> 00:20:10.410
All right!

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.130
What? It is you?

00:20:20.810 --> 00:20:25.370
It's not very cute, but maybe Heidi will like him.

00:20:29.540 --> 00:20:31.370
Hey, stay still!

00:20:47.870 --> 00:20:49.630
I'm back, Joseph!

00:20:56.570 --> 00:20:57.690
Peter.

00:20:59.070 --> 00:21:00.260
Heidi.

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:14.880
Sorry about yesterday.
I caught a bird that looks like Pichi for you.

00:21:18.840 --> 00:21:19.710
Here!

00:21:20.880 --> 00:21:22.060
Peter...

00:21:27.030 --> 00:21:28.290
Thank you.

00:21:36.200 --> 00:21:37.430
Then, goodbye.

00:21:38.280 --> 00:21:39.320
Wait!

00:21:40.520 --> 00:21:41.740
Hold him a little.

00:21:45.670 --> 00:21:47.260
This is for you.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:48.940
Currants.

00:21:49.310 --> 00:21:50.300
And also...

00:21:54.560 --> 00:21:58.290
Me and grandfather found this.
Come on, open your bag.

00:22:03.150 --> 00:22:04.370
That much?

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:06.370
Yes.

00:22:07.970 --> 00:22:11.100
I was angry with you earlier.

00:22:11.320 --> 00:22:12.480
I'm sorry.

00:22:12.770 --> 00:22:15.340
Don't worry.
Thank you, Heidi.

00:22:15.480 --> 00:22:16.770
Then, goodbye.

00:22:18.400 --> 00:22:20.180
Goodbye!

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:21.480
Goodbye!

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:33.100
The Goat General Peter

00:22:25.340 --> 00:22:33.100
Yagi no taishou peetaa

00:22:30.020 --> 00:22:31.560
So warm.

00:22:32.160 --> 00:22:34.550
He really looks like Pichi.

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:42.080
He can get angry, but is truly kind-hearted.

00:22:34.010 --> 00:22:42.080
Okottemo honto ha yasashii peetaa

00:22:35.220 --> 00:22:37.140
I'm glad for you, Heidi.

00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:39.930
I will make it a very beautiful house.

00:22:41.310 --> 00:22:42.650
But...

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:48.640
The two of us shared and ate

00:22:42.870 --> 00:22:48.640
Futari de chiizu to pan wo

00:22:43.170 --> 00:22:44.490
What's wrong?

00:22:45.070 --> 00:22:48.710
Does he also wants to go
somewhere warmer during the winter?

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:53.200
cheese and bread together,

00:22:48.720 --> 00:22:53.200
Wakete tabeta no ne

00:22:50.310 --> 00:22:51.730
I suppose so.

00:22:51.730 --> 00:22:52.810
Really?

00:22:55.530 --> 00:23:05.820
on the day the bellflowers swayed.

00:22:55.530 --> 00:23:05.820
Tsuri ga nesou ga yureteita hi

00:22:55.530 --> 00:23:05.820
Tsuri ga nesou ga yureteita hi

00:22:56.190 --> 00:22:58.510
Then I don't want to keep him.

00:22:58.510 --> 00:23:01.100
He will be much happier with his friends.

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:02.660
Isn't that right, little bird?

00:23:06.550 --> 00:23:08.880
I will apologize to Peter tomorrow.

00:23:10.750 --> 00:23:13.290
Go, your friends are waiting for you.

00:23:30.720 --> 00:23:32.140
Goodbye...

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:33.790
Pichi.

00:23:53.930 --> 00:23:57.500
<i>The harsh winter comes to Alm Mountain.</i>

00:23:57.500 --> 00:24:01.220
<i>The cabin is entirely covered in snow.</i>

00:24:01.220 --> 00:24:05.280
<i>Heidi can't meet with Peter and Snowflake anymore.</i>

00:24:05.300 --> 00:24:07.270
<i>Although it's a bit lonely,</i>

00:24:07.270 --> 00:24:09.520
<i>she helps Grandfather</i>

00:24:09.520 --> 00:24:13.210
<i>to take care of the wild animals
who gather under the big tree,</i>

00:24:13.210 --> 00:24:15.980
<i>during her first winter.</i>

00:24:16.310 --> 00:24:19.350
<i>One day, a snow covered Peter</i>

00:24:19.350 --> 00:24:22.300
<i>comes to visit Heidi.</i>

00:24:22.300 --> 00:24:27.160
<i>A warm fire is blazing in
the cabin on Alm Mountain.</i>

00:24:27.380 --> 00:24:29.900
<i>Next episode:
Silver-White Alms</i>

00:24:29.900 --> 00:24:31.900
<i>Please look forward to it!</i>

